cinema_0 Quick one, I've been doing a live French cinema and music class on Zoom, and it's the best thing I've signed up for this year.
cinema_1 It's Culture Capsules by the French Atelier. 10 live sessions from France taught in English. One hour each plus Q&A.
cinema_2 The theme is cinema and music, how French film and song conquered America. Méliès, Piaf, Aznavour, Gainsbourg, the Nouvelle Vague.
cinema_3 Last week was 8th Piaf. The speaker played the records and told the story behind each one. I've had La Vie en Rose stuck in my head ever since.
cinema_4 Coming up, Bardot and the New Wave, Delaun and Melville, Amélie and Jan Tiersen, and the French composers behind Hollywood.
cinema_5 It's from $63 a month per capsule, three payments. You choose one, two, or all three worlds.
cinema_6 one evening a week, one hour live from France and English and you can ask them anything. Honestly, it's the best thing I've signed up for this year.
fashion_0 Okay, I have to tell you about the class I'm taking on Zoom. It's called Culture Capsules from the French Atelier. It's live from France.
fashion_1 It's 10 live sessions, one a week, with a real French expert, and it's all in English. I don't speak a word of French, and that's fine.
fashion_2 My capsule is fashion and art. How France invented elegance from Versailles to Chanel. Louis XIV, Monet, Dior, Saint Laurent, Gaultier.
fashion_3 Last week was Coco Chanel. The little black dress, no five, the chain strap, how she basically rewrote what women wear, I had chills.
fashion_4 Every session is an hour, and then you ask your questions live. I asked about the Met Gala, and she had an answer for me on the spot.
fashion_5 It's from $6.3 a month per capsule, three payments. Honestly, that's less than my Friday dinner out.
fashion_6 If you've ever stood in a museum wishing someone would just explain it to you, this is that. Go look at the French Atelier site, Culture Capsules.
gastro_0 I haven't. I'm taking a French gastronomy class, live from France, on Zoom.
gastro_1 It's the French Atelier's Culture Capsules. Ten live sessions, one a week, with a French export, and it's all in English.
gastro_2 The theme is gastronomy and wine, why the French table is law, history, and identity. The baguette, salted butter, camembert, champagne.
gastro_3 Last week was the baguette. There is literally a long about what goes in it. Four ingredients, that's it, my mind.
gastro_4 Next is champagne, then the macaron, then the black truffle, and after each hour you ask the expert anything you want, live.
gastro_5 It's from $6 to $3 a month per capsule, three monthly payments. And you can pick one capsule, two, or all three.
gastro_6 If you love food and wine and actually knowing why things taste the way they do, go to the French Atelier site, Culture Capsules.
